<section data-screen-label="Which treatment is best" id="best-treatment" style="background:var(--white);border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:clamp(32px,4vw,64px);align-items:start;margin-bottom:clamp(36px,4vw,56px)">
<div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Product comparison</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink-950)">Which Stem Cell Treatment Is Best for Knee Osteoarthritis?</h2>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Current evidence does not establish one universally superior cell source, product or dose.</strong> A 2026 network meta-analysis suggested possible differences between cell sources and doses, but indirect cross-study comparisons are not strong enough to establish a universal winner.<a href="#ref-6" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">6</a></p>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Claims such as “umbilical cells are best,” “adipose is best,” or “100 million cells is the optimal dose” therefore go beyond what the evidence currently supports.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(270px,1fr));gap:24px">
<article style="border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);background:var(--paper)">
<span style="display:inline-flex;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Example A</span>
<div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:30px;line-height:1.1;margin:22px 0 10px;color:var(--ink-950)">Donor MSCs</div>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">A manufactured donor-derived cell product.</p>
<ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:20px 0 0">
<li style="padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Need to verify:</strong> product identity</li>
<li style="padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Need to verify:</strong> manufacturing &amp; viability</li>
<li style="padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Need to verify:</strong> diagnosis-specific evidence</li>
</ul>
</article>
<article style="border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);background:var(--paper)">
<span style="display:inline-flex;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Example B</span>
<div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:30px;line-height:1.1;margin:22px 0 10px;color:var(--ink-950)">BMAC + PRP</div>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Same-day autologous bone-marrow concentrate plus platelet-rich plasma.</p>
<ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:20px 0 0">
<li style="padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Need to verify:</strong> processing method</li>
<li style="padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Need to verify:</strong> cell/product characterization</li>
<li style="padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Need to verify:</strong> why combination is proposed</li>
</ul>
</article>
<article style="border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);background:var(--paper)">
<span style="display:inline-flex;padding:6px 12px;border-radius:var(--radius-pill);border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Example C</span>
<div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:30px;line-height:1.1;margin:22px 0 10px;color:var(--ink-950)">Expanded MSCs</div>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Culture-expanded cells manufactured before administration.</p>
<ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:20px 0 0">
<li style="padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Need to verify:</strong> source &amp; expansion process</li>
<li style="padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Need to verify:</strong> dose &amp; viability</li>
<li style="padding:11px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:14px;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>Need to verify:</strong> supporting clinical evidence</li>
</ul>
</article>
</div>
<div style="margin-top:24px;border:1px solid var(--line-on-light-strong);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(24px,3vw,32px);display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:24px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between">
<div style="max-width:62ch">
<strong style="display:block;font-family:var(--font-subhead);font-size:20px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink-950)">Which option is actually better?</strong>
<p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">You cannot answer from the headline product name or advertised cell count. Diagnosis, product identity, manufacturing, evidence, delivery and physician rationale all matter.</p>
</div>
<button class="sc-inline-cta on-light" data-stemcierge-quiz="true" type="button">Help Me Compare My Protocol</button>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section data-dark="true" data-screen-label="BMAC vs MSCs" id="bmac-vs-msc" style="background:var(--ink-950);color:var(--white);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto">
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:clamp(32px,4vw,64px);align-items:start;margin-bottom:clamp(36px,4vw,56px)">
<div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-500)">Important distinction</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--white)">BMAC vs Culture-Expanded MSCs: Why the Difference Matters</h2>
</div>
<div>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-dark-secondary)">BMAC is often marketed as “stem-cell therapy,” but it is a mixed bone-marrow concentrate. Culture-expanded MSC therapy involves isolating and expanding cells under controlled manufacturing conditions. Evidence from one should not automatically be transferred to the other.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:24px">
<article data-light="true" style="background:var(--white);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(26px,3vw,34px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card-dark)">
<h3 style="margin:0 0 14px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:28px;line-height:1.1;color:var(--ink-950)">BMAC</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Same-day concentrated bone marrow containing many cell populations and biological components.</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 18px;padding-left:20px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">
<li style="margin:8px 0">heterogeneous product</li>
<li style="margin:8px 0">composition can vary</li>
<li style="margin:8px 0">not purified MSC therapy</li>
<li style="margin:8px 0">randomized evidence shows symptom improvement but no clear clinically meaningful superiority over comparator injections</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin:0;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">A systematic review of eight RCTs involving 937 patients found improvements from baseline, but between-group differences generally did not exceed minimal clinically important thresholds.<a href="#ref-7" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">7</a></p>
</article>
<article data-light="true" style="background:var(--white);border-radius:8px;padding:clamp(26px,3vw,34px);box-shadow:var(--shadow-card-dark)">
<h3 style="margin:0 0 14px;font-family:var(--font-display);font-weight:400;font-size:28px;line-height:1.1;color:var(--ink-950)">Culture-expanded MSCs</h3>
<p style="margin:0 0 16px;font-size:16px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">Cells are isolated and expanded outside the body before administration, producing a more extensively manufactured product.</p>
<ul style="margin:0 0 18px;padding-left:20px;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">
<li style="margin:8px 0">different manufacturing requirements</li>
<li style="margin:8px 0">source may be bone marrow, adipose or donor tissue</li>
<li style="margin:8px 0">dose and product characterization can be more explicit</li>
<li style="margin:8px 0">regulatory status varies by country and product</li>
</ul>
<p style="margin:0;padding-top:18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">A 2026 MILES single-cell analysis also found substantial site-to-site variability in BMAC composition, reinforcing why product labels alone are not enough.<a href="#ref-8" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">8</a></p>
</article>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section data-screen-label="PRP" id="prp" style="background:var(--white);border-top:1px solid var(--line-on-light);padding:clamp(56px,7vw,104px) 0;scroll-margin-top:120px">
<div style="width:min(100% - clamp(64px,14vw,128px),1200px);margin-inline:auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:clamp(32px,4vw,64px);align-items:stretch">
<div>
<span style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 18px;padding-top:14px;border-top:2px solid var(--sand-500);font-size:11px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:var(--ls-eyebrow);text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sand-700)">Another orthobiologic</span>
<h2 style="margin:0;font-family:var(--font-body);font-weight:700;font-size:clamp(31px,3.9vw,52px);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:var(--ink-950)">What About PRP for Knee Osteoarthritis?</h2>
<p style="margin:22px 0 18px;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)"><strong>PRP is not a stem-cell treatment.</strong> It is produced from concentrated platelets in blood and belongs to the broader orthobiologics/regenerative-medicine category.</p>
<p style="margin:0 0 18px;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">AAOS states that PRP may reduce pain and improve function in symptomatic knee OA, but the recommendation strength is limited because studies are heterogeneous.<a href="#ref-9" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">9</a> A 2025 placebo-controlled meta-analysis of 11 RCTs and 1,616 participants found pain benefits at three and six months but not at 12 months, with weaker and less durable functional findings.<a href="#ref-10" style="font-size:.72em;vertical-align:super;margin-left:2px">10</a></p>
<p style="margin:0;max-width:64ch;font-size:17px;line-height:1.72;color:var(--text-on-light-secondary)">The practical lesson is simple: a clinic offering PRP and a clinic offering culture-expanded MSCs are not offering two versions of the same treatment.</p>
</div>
<div style="min-height:320px;height:100%;border:1px solid var(--line-on-light);border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--paper)">
